      "writtenOn": "2024-02-13T18:57:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Wonsik,\n\nI prefer to keep this API in Android instead of moving it to support library. We have existing API `setParameter()` and we respect its nature of being sticky. And We will add this new API `setParameterDeferred()` and this one will be non-sticky, which will take effect only at the given timestamp. I think this is full functionality for users\u0027 control flow for both sticky and non-sticky configurations. Otherwise, I don\u0027t this it is a good user experience to have to rely on support library for non-sticky configurations.\n\nAlso, I think this API is not only target at ROI, but other run-time non-sticky configurations. E.g. dynamic HDR info or other may be added in the future.",
      "parentUuid": "60e404df_dc6d7cef",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5061,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 5061,
        "endChar": 4
      },
      "revId": "1132619d35d2868b1d9bceb45c4ad055427e468b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "84a8e71e_2a89b185",
        "filename": "media/java/android/media/MediaCodec.java",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 5061,
      "author": {
        "id": 1018606
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-13T19:32:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e We have existing API setParameter() and we respect its nature of being sticky. And We will add this new API setParameterDeferred() and this one will be non-sticky, which will take effect only at the given timestamp.\n\nIn current implementation it _is_ sticky after the specified timestamp, as it just calls `setParameter` at the given timestamp. The name of the API and the documentation also do not mention about the stickiness of the parameter. I\u0027m happy to discuss transient / sticky parameters for the buffer, but at current form it seems to be out of scope of this API.",
      "parentUuid": "343beae2_b12fe5de",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5061,
        "startChar": 0,
